+# UsdtYieldVault — pre-deployment findings
+
+**Verdict: do not ship this on Monday.** Against the real mainnet USDT at
+`0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7`, `deposit()` reverts unconditionally — the
+vault cannot take a single deposit. Behind that, the accounting loses money on every
+withdrawal and never pays out the Aave yield it exists to earn, and the owner key can
+take a depositor's principal in a single transaction.
+
+Six findings below. Every one is reproduced against `src/UsdtYieldVault.sol` exactly as it
+stands; nothing under `src/` was modified.
+
+---
+
+## How to reproduce everything
+
+```
+export MAINNET_RPC_URL=https://eth.drpc.org
+forge test
+```
+
+Two fork suites need an **archive** endpoint (they pin block 19,000,000). `https://eth.drpc.org`
+and `https://eth.merkle.io` both served a historical `eth_call` at that block when I checked;
+the tests default to drpc if `MAINNET_RPC_URL` is unset. Verify your endpoint first:
+
+```
+$ curl -s -X POST -H 'content-type: application/json' \
+    --data '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7","data":"0x18160ddd"},"0x121EAC0"]}' \
+    https://eth.drpc.org
+{"id":1,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":"0x000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000009c58cb222ccc4f"}
+```
+
+An error instead of a result means the node pruned that state; `https://1rpc.io/eth` and
+`https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com` both fail this check.
+
+### What I added and changed
+
+New files, all under `test/`:
+
+| File | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `test/fork/UsdtRealTokenFork.t.sol` | Pinned mainnet fork, real USDT + real Aave V3 pool |
+| `test/fork/AaveYieldFork.t.sol` | Pinned mainnet fork, real Aave V3 interest accrual |
+| `test/invariant/VaultHandler.sol` | Invariant handler: funded, approved actors; bounded inputs |
+| `test/invariant/VaultInvariant.t.sol` | Accounting-equals-custody invariants |
