+## Why the existing suite is green
+
+The 39 passing tests and the 100% figure are real, and they are compatible with every bug below.
+
+```
+$ forge coverage --match-path 'test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol' --no-match-coverage 'test/'
+...
+Suite result: ok. 39 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 8.82ms (74.68ms CPU time)
+
+Ran 1 test suite in 11.35ms (8.82ms CPU time): 39 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (39 total tests)
+
+╭------------------------+-----------------+----------------+--------------+-----------------╮
+| File                   | % Lines         | % Statements   | % Branches   | % Funcs         |
++============================================================================================+
+| src/UsdtYieldVault.sol | 100.00% (52/52) | 98.25% (56/57) | 85.71% (6/7) | 100.00% (11/11) |
+|------------------------+-----------------+----------------+--------------+-----------------|
+| Total                  | 100.00% (52/52) | 98.25% (56/57) | 85.71% (6/7) | 100.00% (11/11) |
+╰------------------------+-----------------+----------------+--------------+-----------------╯
+```
+
+Coverage records which lines executed. It never records whether an assertion *could* have
+failed. Structurally, the suite performs none of the three searches this contract needs:
+
+- **It is all mocks.** `MockUSDT` is a stock OpenZeppelin `ERC20`, which returns `bool` from
+  `approve`. Real USDT does not. The mock encodes the assumption; testing against it only
+  re-tests the assumption. That is finding **F-1**, and it is fatal.
+- **Many tests assert the implementation back to itself.** `test_ConstructorSetsUsdt`,
+  `test_BpsDenominator`, `test_ShareScale`, `test_MinDeposit`, `test_WithdrawFeeBps`,
+  `test_SetDepositFeeUpdatesValue`, `test_DepositUpdatesTotalShares`,
+  `test_ConvertToSharesAfterDeposit` and friends check a getter against the constant or the
+  argument that was just written into it. They execute lines and constrain nothing.
+- **Every test exercises one or two operations in isolation.** `test_PartialWithdraw` is the
+  deepest sequence in the file. The accounting bug in **F-3** is invisible to any such test
+  because it accumulates: each withdrawal is individually "correct", and the gap only becomes
+  obvious across a sequence.
+- **`depositFeeBps` is only ever set to `10` or `0`.** Both walk the same branch. The domain
+  `setDepositFee` actually accepts is `[0, 2**256-1]` — see **F-4**.
+- **No test moves time forward.** Yield is the entire product, and nothing in the suite ever
+  lets a second pass — see **F-2**.
+
+I also tried to run `slither .` as a cross-check. The installed binary is broken on this
+machine (`ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'slither'`), so **the static-analysis item is
+not done** — worth running on a working install before sign-off, though nothing below depends
+on it.
