+## F-2 — CRITICAL: the vault earns Aave yield and no depositor can ever claim it. A one-year deposit loses money.
+
+`totalAssetsStored` is a plain counter, incremented on deposit and decremented on withdrawal.
+`totalAssets()` returns it verbatim. Nothing in the contract ever reads
+`aUsdt.balanceOf(address(this))`. aTokens are rebasing: the vault's real balance grows every
+second, and the vault's idea of its own balance does not. `convertToAssets` prices shares off
+`totalAssetsStored`, so the yield is never reflected in anybody's redeemable value.
+
+The result: a depositor who leaves funds in for a year gets back **less than they put in**,
+because the 0.30% withdrawal fee is charged and the yield is not paid.
+
+This test runs against the **real Aave V3 pool** at `0x87870Bca3F3fD6335C3F4ce8392D69350B4fA4E2`
+on a pinned fork. It uses real USDC rather than real USDT purely because F-1 makes USDT
+undepositable — the pool, the aToken and the interest accrual are the genuine mainnet ones,
+and the accounting defect is in the vault, not in the token.
+
+```
+$ export MAINNET_RPC_URL=https://eth.drpc.org
+$ forge test --match-path 'test/fork/AaveYieldFork.t.sol' -vv
+Ran 2 tests for test/fork/AaveYieldFork.t.sol:AaveYieldForkTest
+[FAIL: depositor got back less than principal after a year of yield: 9970000000 <= 10000000000] test_InterestIsStrandedOnExit() (gas: 434510)
+Logs:
+  alice deposited               10000000000
+  alice received after 1 year   9970000000
+  aToken left in vault          672500711
+  vault totalShares             0
+
+[FAIL: depositor's redeemable value did not grow with the interest the vault earned: 10000000000 < 10642500711] test_YieldAccruesToDepositors() (gas: 371923)
+Logs:
+  aToken held at deposit        10000000000
+  aToken held after 365 days    10642500711
+  real interest earned          642500711
+  vault.totalAssets()           10000000000
+  alice balanceOfUnderlying()   10000000000
+
+Suite result: FAILED. 0 passed; 2 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 9.99s (15.61s CPU time)
+
+Ran 1 test suite in 10.00s (9.99s CPU time): 0 tests passed, 2 failed, 0 skipped (2 total tests)
+```
+
+Read the second block: the vault's aToken balance went from 10,000.00 to 10,642.50 — Aave paid
+642.50 of real interest — while `totalAssets()` and `balanceOfUnderlying(alice)` both sat at
+exactly 10,000.00. In the first block, Alice deposits 10,000, waits a year, burns every share
+she owns, and receives 9,970. She is down 30. Meanwhile 672.50 of aUSDC remains in the vault
+with `totalShares == 0`: nobody holds a claim on it, and the next depositor starts from a fresh
+share price, so it is unreachable forever.
+
+A "yield vault" that pays negative yield is not a bug in a corner of the product. It is the
+product.
+
+**Fix.** Delete `totalAssetsStored` and derive assets from custody:
+`function totalAssets() public view returns (uint256) { return aUsdt.balanceOf(address(this)); }`.
+`convertToShares` / `convertToAssets` then price against the live aToken balance and yield
+accrues to shareholders automatically. This also removes the class of bug in F-3 by
+construction — there is no second copy of the balance to drift. Since the vault then becomes
+donation-priced, add the standard first-depositor protections at the same time: virtual
+shares/assets (as in OpenZeppelin's ERC4626) or a dead-shares mint on the first deposit.
+The cleanest route overall is to inherit OpenZeppelin's `ERC4626` and override
+`totalAssets()`, which also gives depositors a transferable share token — right now
+`shareBalance` is a bare mapping with no transfer function at all.
+
